{"type":"message","id":"ad8421d9","parentId":"9ffe2d92","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:31:57.340Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-17 23:01 GMT+5:30] Implement the safest stability fixes from the root cause analysis, with backup and rollback.\n\n**Goal**: Improve gateway stability and reduce rate limit disruptions with minimal risk.\n\n**Safe fixes to apply (in order):**\n\n1. **WebSocket keepalive tuning** — add ping/pong intervals to prevent NAT timeouts\n   - Locate WebSocket server creation (likely in `dist/entry.js` or `src/ws-server.ts`)\n   - Set: `pingInterval: 30000`, `pingTimeout: 10000`\n   - This is low-risk and often helps\n\n2. **OpenRouter retry/backoff** — handle 429 responses gracefully\n   - Find OpenRouter provider code: `src/providers/openrouter.ts` or similar\n   - Add: detect 429, read `Retry-After` header, exponential backoff with jitter\n   - Also add config: `models.providers.openrouter.maxRetries: 3` and `backoffMs: 1000`\n   - This may require careful editing but is contained to one provider\n\n3. **Gateway lock cleanup** — make startup more robust\n   - Review lock handling code (likely `src/gateway/lock.ts` or similar)\n   - On startup, check if lock PID is still running; if not, auto-clear\n   - This prevents stale lock delays\n\n**Before making changes:**\n- Create a backup of the current config and affected source files\n- Document what will be changed and why\n- Prepare rollback steps (git revert or restore backups)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n1. Summary of changes made\n2. File diffs or descriptions\n3. Verification steps to confirm fixes are working\n4. Any config updates needed to enable/disable features\n\n**Caution:** Only apply changes that are clearly reversible and well-understood. If any change requires complex modifications or could break running services, skip it and report why. Prioritize stability over completeness.\n\nWork in the OpenClaw project at `D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw`. Use your best judgment and be meticulous."}],"timestamp":1771349517337}}
{"type":"message","id":"3ccd76c2","parentId":"ad8421d9","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:32:02.995Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll implement these stability fixes systematically, starting with creating backups and then applying each fix in order of safety and impact.\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-9fc20e91-b403-4df9-b3e9-e4e1cadb2a1d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"git status","env":{"CI":"true","DEBIAN_FRONTEND":"noninteractive","GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT":"0","GCM_INTERACTIVE":"never","HOMEBREW_NO_AUTO_UPDATE":"1","GIT_EDITOR":"true","EDITOR":"true","VISUAL":"true","GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR":"true","GIT_PAGER":"cat","PAGER":"cat","npm_config_yes":"true","PIP_NO_INPUT":"1","YARN_ENABLE_IMMUTABLE_INSTALLS":"false"}}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"arcee-ai/trinity-large-preview:free","usage":{"input":11206,"output":165,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11371,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771349517340}}
